1. ARCHITECTURE AUDIT — Review against OWASP Top 10 + OWASP API Security Top 10
2. AUTH — httpOnly cookies, JWT rotation, refresh token rotation, 
   session kill on deactivation, concurrent session limits, MFA ready
3. AUTHORIZATION — RLS on every Supabase table, IDOR checks on 
   every endpoint, no horizontal privilege escalation possible, 
   mass assignment protection
4. INPUT SECURITY — sanitize + validate all inputs with zod, 
   parameterized queries only, no raw SQL
5. RATE LIMITING — on auth, on all API endpoints, on bulk actions
6. SECURITY HEADERS — CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, 
   X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy
7. DATA PROTECTION — encrypt sensitive PII fields, 
   mask data by role, never expose raw DB errors
8. INFRASTRUCTURE — no secrets in code, HTTPS only, 
   CORS locked to exact domain
9. MONITORING — log all auth events, role changes, 
   data exports with timestamps and IPs
10. DEPENDENCY SAFETY — flag any package with known CVEs

After building, generate:
- A security checklist with PASS/FAIL for each item
- A list of anything that needs manual review
- Recommended security headers config
